{"Title":"An Act authorizing the town of Shrewsbury to grant abatement of real estate taxes for the daughter of fallen firefighter Christopher Roy","BillNumber":"H3906","DocketNumber":"HD4369","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"HEK1","Name":"Hannah Kane","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/HEK1","ResponseDate":"2023-05-31T10:10:52.22"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"HEK1","Name":"Hannah Kane","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/HEK1","ResponseDate":"2023-05-31T10:10:52.22"},{"Id":"MOM0","Name":"Michael O. Moore","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/MOM0","ResponseDate":"2023-05-31T11:40:05.8233333"}],"JointSponsor":{"Id":"MOM0","Name":"Michael O. Moore","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/MOM0","ResponseDate":"2023-05-31T10:10:52.22"},"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H3906/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Kane of Shrewsbury and Senator Moore, a joint petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 3906) of Hannah Kane and Michael O. Moore (by vote of the town) that the town of Shrewsbury be authorized to grant abatement of certain real estate taxes for the daughter of fallen firefighter Christopher Roy.  Revenue.  [Local Approval Received.]","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1.  Notwithstanding Section 5 of Chapter 59 of the general laws or any general or special law to the contrary, the Board of Assessors of the Town of Shrewsbury shall grant abatement of the real estate taxes assessed for tax years 2024 through 2036, inclusive, upon real property that is (i) the domicile of Ava Roy, the surviving daughter of Christopher Roy, a firefighter killed in the line of duty; and (ii) owned by and occupied as the domicile of the guardian, trustee, conservator, adoptive parent or other fiduciary for Ava Roy.\r\n\tSECTION 2.  This act shall take effect upon its passage.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[{"Description":"Home Rule","DownloadUrl":"http://malegislature.gov/api/DownloadReport?attachmentId=16945&title=Home%20Rule"}],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Favorable","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J26","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J26"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Place in OD","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"H52","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/H52"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Correctly Drawn","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"H36","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/H36"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Correctly Drawn","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"S31","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/S31"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}